<title>NORWAY: AKER RGI TAKES H1 OPERATING LOSS.</title>
<headline>AKER RGI TAKES H1 OPERATING LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Turnover			     12,009    vs	9,514</p>
<p> Operating result	     minus  237    vs	  288</p>
<p> Result after financial items	284    vs	  257</p>
<p> Net result				308    vs	   71</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norwegian industrial holding company is AKER RGI ASA, which has major shareholdings in Norwegian Seafoods ASA, Aker Maritime ASA and Scancem AB.</p>
<p>The company was established last year after Resource Group International (RGI) merged with engineering and construction group AKER ASA. Comparative 1996 figures were calculated on a pro forma basis.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
